# SQLFluff's dbt templater can't lint macro files at all — a macro has no
# compiled SQL node in the dbt manifest (it's a Jinja template definition,
# not a query dbt runs), so the templater skips it outright. Excluding it
# here makes that a deliberate, silent exclusion instead of a WARNING on
# every lint run. This is SQLFluff's own documented recommendation for
# dbt projects, not a gap in test coverage.
macros/
